		{
			title: "Unknown Quantity"
			x: 1.0d
			y: 3.25d
			shape: "pentagon"
			description: [
				"&dHuh... is that the same Voxxulon? Or did someone new take the Boss position?"
				""
				"&5No idea, but that isn't who it used to be. The previous Vox Ponds boss used to be a middle manager for the FOP. "
				""
				"&dKept himself 'necessary' by inciting distrust and rivalries between management above him, and subordinates below him. Was really good at it, while keeping out of the crossfire."
				""
				"&5He was really really good at gaslighting and playing office politics, becoming more and more toxic as he played his own little power game."
				""
				"&dWonder if someone finally caught wind of him after he took over the Vox Ponds boss position."
			]
			dependencies: ["79F4AD48FC07AC72"]
			id: "2F14B55DDA9D522D"
			tasks: [{
				id: "679477C6899DF98B"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "A New Level of Vile"
			x: 3.25d
			y: 3.25d
			shape: "hexagon"
			description: [
				"&5Okay, poking into things, it seems we were right. It IS the same Voxxulon, just their new position of power has... well..."
				""
				"&dTwisted them into an even more vile thing. They aren't even the same Voxxulon model from before, it seems they've changed and shifted it into some weird, horrible shape."
				""
				"&5I'm afraid there isn't much of a choice in dealing with Voxxulon, Bandit. Start prepping some anti-poison gear and protection, we haven't found a way around this twisted boss."
				""
				"&dYou'll also want a Vile Stone, which you can get by smelting a bucket of Toxic Water in a furnace."
			]
			dependencies: ["2F14B55DDA9D522D"]
			id: "329AAEAD023CD38F"
			tasks: [{
				id: "522E228F7484A48A"
				type: "item"
				item: "aoa3:vile_stone"
